### Perrubi API - Requests de prueba
### Requiere la extensión "REST Client" de VSCode (Huachao Mao).
### Con el server corriendo (`node app.js` / `npm run dev`), abrí este archivo
### y hacé click en "Send Request" arriba de cada bloque (empezando por los logins).
### Las variables @userToken / @walkerToken se completan solas con la respuesta del login.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### =========================================================
### AUTH
### =========================================================

### Registrar un User (dueño de perro)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/userRegister
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Juan",
  "lastName": "Sabio",
  "email": "noahtest1@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}

### Registrar un Walker (paseador)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/walkerRegister
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Pedro",
  "lastName": "Paseador",
  "email": "pedrotest1@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}

### Login como User -> guarda el token en @userToken
# @name userLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/userLogin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "noahtest1@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}

###

@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.token}}

### Login como Walker -> guarda el token en @walkerToken
# @name walkerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/walkerLogin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "pedrotest1@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}

###

@walkerToken = {{walkerLogin.response.body.token}}

### Ver mi perfil (User)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Ver mi perfil (Walker)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{walkerToken}}

### Actualizar mi perfil
PUT {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Juan Editado"
}

### Cambiar mi contraseña
PUT {{baseUrl}}/auth/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "123456",
  "newPassword": "123456"
}


### =========================================================
### DOGS
### =========================================================

### Crear un perro (como User) -> guarda el id en @dogId
# @name createDog
POST {{baseUrl}}/dogs
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Firulais",
  "breed": "Labrador",
  "age": 3,
  "gender": "M",
  "weight": 25.5,
  "extraNotes": "Muy amigable"
}

###

@dogId = {{createDog.response.body.id}}

### Mis perros (como User)
GET {{baseUrl}}/dogs/user
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Actualizar un perro
PUT {{baseUrl}}/dogs/{{dogId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Firulais Editado",
  "weight": 26
}

### Borrar un perro
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/dogs/{{dogId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Todos los perros (requiere admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/dogs
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Perros de un usuario puntual (requiere admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/dogs/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### =========================================================
### ADDRESSES
### =========================================================

### Crear dirección con calle (geocodifica con Google Maps)
# @name createAddress
POST {{baseUrl}}/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "Casa",
  "street": "Galván",
  "number": "3124",
  "city": "CABA",
  "zipCode": "C1431"
}

###

@addressId = {{createAddress.response.body.id}}

### Crear dirección con coordenadas directas
POST {{baseUrl}}/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "Trabajo",
  "latitude": -34.5667227,
  "longitude": -58.4877776
}

### Mis direcciones
GET {{baseUrl}}/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Actualizar dirección
PUT {{baseUrl}}/addresses/{{addressId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "Casa editada"
}

### Borrar dirección
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/addresses/{{addressId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### =========================================================
### WALKS
### =========================================================

### Crear un paseo (requiere tener al menos un perro creado, ver @dogId arriba)
# @name createWalk
POST {{baseUrl}}/walks
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dogIds": [{{dogId}}],
  "walkType": "individual",
  "startTime": "2026-08-08T15:00:00.000Z",
  "duration": 30
}

###

@walkId = 14

### Mis paseos (User o Walker, según el token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/walks/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Paseos disponibles para tomar (Walker)
GET {{baseUrl}}/walks/available
Authorization: Bearer {{walkerToken}}

### Ver un paseo puntual
GET {{baseUrl}}/walks/{{walkId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Editar un paseo (solo mientras está en estado "searching")
PUT {{baseUrl}}/walks/{{walkId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "duration": 45
}

### Aceptar un paseo (Walker)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/walks/{{walkId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{walkerToken}}

### Cambiar estado de un paseo
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/walks/{{walkId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{walkerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "finished"
}

### Todos los paseos (requiere admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/walks
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### =========================================================
### CHAT (exclusivo del paseo, entre el usuario dueño y el paseador asignado)
### Se abre al aceptar el paseo (PATCH /walks/{{walkId}}/accept) y se cierra
### (solo lectura) cuando el paseo pasa a un estado final (finished/canceled).
### =========================================================

### Ver el chat de un paseo (requiere que ya haya paseador asignado)
GET {{baseUrl}}/walks/{{walkId}}/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Enviar un mensaje (User)
POST {{baseUrl}}/walks/{{walkId}}/chat/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Hola! Firulais ya está en la puerta"
}

### Enviar un mensaje (Walker)
POST {{baseUrl}}/walks/{{walkId}}/chat/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{walkerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Perfecto, llego en 5 minutos"
}

### Marcar como leídos los mensajes del otro participante
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/walks/{{walkId}}/chat/read
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### =========================================================
### MAPS
### =========================================================

### Geocodificar una dirección de texto -> devuelve lat/long
POST {{baseUrl}}/maps/directions
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "textQuery": "Galván 3124, CABA"
}

### Calcular ruta a pie entre dos coordenadas (obtenidas con /maps/directions)
POST {{baseUrl}}/maps/route
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "origin": {
    "location": {
      "latLng": {
        "latitude": -34.5667227,
        "longitude": -58.4877776
      }
    }
  },
  "destination": {
    "location": {
      "latLng": {
        "latitude": -34.5735,
        "longitude": -58.4361
      }
    }
  }
}


### =========================================================
### IA (matching, recomendaciones, reseñas)
### Necesita el microservicio de Python corriendo en paralelo:
###   cd "Perrubi- Parte IA" && python -m uvicorn api:app --port 8000
### =========================================================

### Crear una reseña (User) — el @walkId de la sección WALKS tiene que estar
### en estado "finished" antes de poder calificarlo (aceptar -> in_progress
### -> finished, con los requests de la sección WALKS de arriba).
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "walkId": {{walkId}},
  "rating": 2,
  "comment": "Llegó tarde y el perro volvió sucio"
}

### Ver el resumen de rating de un paseador puntual (cambiar el 1 por el id
### real del walker, lo ves en la respuesta del walkerLogin de arriba)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reviews/walker/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Paseadores con mala calificación (requiere una cuenta con role "admin")
GET {{baseUrl}}/reviews/low-quality
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Buscar paseadores por matching — necesita que el Walker de prueba tenga
### latitude/longitude/tags y al menos una fila en WalkerAvailability
### cargados a mano en Prisma Studio (ver guía de pasos).
POST {{baseUrl}}/matching/walkers
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "latitude": -34.60,
  "longitude": -58.38,
  "startMinutes": 540,
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "needs": ["perro_grande", "adiestramiento"],
  "maxDistanceKm": 5
}

### Recomendaciones de paseadores — necesita que el User de prueba tenga
### "likes" cargados a mano en Prisma Studio (ver guía de pasos).
GET {{baseUrl}}/recommendations/walkers?topN=5
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
